(7640046, 1240318, 101668, '<td valign="top">So so pretty</td>', 'So so pretty', '2019-09-01 06:05:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640252, 1240318, 6804, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful rendition of Boats The watercolor sky is perfect.  Youve done a great job keeping the diagonal lines (ropes) from going jagged.  This is excellent work!</td>', 'This is a beautiful rendition of Boats The watercolor sky is perfect.  Youve done a great job keeping the diagonal lines (ropes) from going jagged.  This is excellent work!', '2019-09-03 03:13:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640253, 1240395, 6804, '<td valign="top">Your colors are great here!  Strong, very rich but not over-done. The composition is just lacking a little interest for me.  I think if I suggest that you move left or right to try to get a third boat into the shot,  you may be limited by the end of the dock you are shooting from.  I think if you were shooting from a kayak or something more mobile,  You might have had an easier time positioning the shot.  I hope this is helpful and not too critical.  The technical aspects of the shot are excellent.</td>', 'Your colors are great here!  Strong, very rich but not over-done. The composition is just lacking a little interest for me.  I think if I suggest that you move left or right to try to get a third boat into the shot,  you may be limited by the end of the dock you are shooting from.  I think if you were shooting from a kayak or something more mobile,  You might have had an easier time positioning the shot.  I hope this is helpful and not too critical.  The technical aspects of the shot are excellent.', '2019-09-03 03:24:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640254, 1240269, 6804, '<td valign="top">Pretty tricky!  Creating a "Boat"    It will probably cost you some votes from the viewers who don''t play cards.   The image is great!  I do like the dark shadows that force your eyes back to the center of the shot.  I love the wrinkle in the cloth and the chips showing just above the white shirt...  (It makes the setting more "real" for me).  The three sets of cards face down on the table, however,  make me feel like you didn''t have enough people to put the cards in the other player''s hands.  If I were hunting for something "wrong" in the shot, that would be it to me...  not horrible,  but just slightly contrived.</td>', 'Pretty tricky!  Creating a "Boat"    It will probably cost you some votes from the viewers who don''t play cards.   The image is great!  I do like the dark shadows that force your eyes back to the center of the shot.  I love the wrinkle in the cloth and the chips showing just above the white shirt...  (It makes the setting more "real" for me).  The three sets of cards face down on the table, however,  make me feel like you didn''t have enough people to put the cards in the other player''s hands.  If I were hunting for something "wrong" in the shot, that would be it to me...  not horrible,  but just slightly contrived.', '2019-09-03 03:36:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640255, 1240411, 6804, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot!  I love the absolutely calm muddy water in this.  Your very long exposure was a great choice.  the soft clouds match the calm water and keep your focus on the ... boat,  is it?  Half of a boat?</td>', 'Interesting shot!  I love the absolutely calm muddy water in this.  Your very long exposure was a great choice.  the soft clouds match the calm water and keep your focus on the ... boat,  is it?  Half of a boat?', '2019-09-03 03:40:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640256, 1240286, 6804, '<td valign="top">Artsy shot!  My favorite part of this is the cloud that looks like a splash hit the sky.   The shadows are just a little heavy for my taste,  but with the added grain it is clearly intentional,  which I like a lot!  Go bold!    My one nit-pick,  If I had to find something to improve on this would be the tilt perspective of the sky-scraper on the far right.  (But after I actually check it, its perfect).   Great job!  I think Blk/Wht was a good choice for this as well.   Good Luck!</td>', 'Artsy shot!  My favorite part of this is the cloud that looks like a splash hit the sky.   The shadows are just a little heavy for my taste,  but with the added grain it is clearly intentional,  which I like a lot!  Go bold!    My one nit-pick,  If I had to find something to improve on this would be the tilt perspective of the sky-scraper on the far right.  (But after I actually check it, its perfect).   Great job!  I think Blk/Wht was a good choice for this as well.   Good Luck!', '2019-09-03 03:47:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640257, 1240374, 6804, '<td valign="top">Awesome!  This is a nice image to see in this challenge!  Excellent composition.  Loaded with movement and interest.  The classic boat in Black/White,  surrounded by wood grain and rust.  All my favorite things to photograph.  You''ve done a stellar job with this one!</td>', 'Awesome!  This is a nice image to see in this challenge!  Excellent composition.  Loaded with movement and interest.  The classic boat in Black/White,  surrounded by wood grain and rust.  All my favorite things to photograph.  You''ve done a stellar job with this one!', '2019-09-03 03:52:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640258, 1240245, 6804, '<td valign="top">Great job of shooting into the sun!  I like the harsh yellow to soft blue sky in this.  The opposing colors of the sky are mirrored in the softness of the boats with the harsh scrapes and rust.  Interesting work!  I think you may get a comment or two telling you to remove the small part of the neighboring boat on the far right of the frame.  I actually like it in there just as you have it.  The boats run in a line and the patch of water at the end makes your eye go up to that mark and throws your eye back on to the boats with the lead-lines created by the clouds.  I enjoyed seeing this!</td>', 'Great job of shooting into the sun!  I like the harsh yellow to soft blue sky in this.  The opposing colors of the sky are mirrored in the softness of the boats with the harsh scrapes and rust.  Interesting work!  I think you may get a comment or two telling you to remove the small part of the neighboring boat on the far right of the frame.  I actually like it in there just as you have it.  The boats run in a line and the patch of water at the end makes your eye go up to that mark and throws your eye back on to the boats with the lead-lines created by the clouds.  I enjoyed seeing this!', '2019-09-03 04:02:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640259, 1240423, 6804, '<td valign="top">Great image!  I like the fog in the background and the extreme clarity in the foreground.  It''s a fun and bright shot!  Nice work!</td>', 'Great image!  I like the fog in the background and the extreme clarity in the foreground.  It''s a fun and bright shot!  Nice work!', '2019-09-03 04:04:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640260, 1240419, 6804, '<td valign="top">Its interesting for me to see how the horizon is tilted to the left so the subject matter at the bottom appears level.  It actually works well in this image.  Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'Its interesting for me to see how the horizon is tilted to the left so the subject matter at the bottom appears level.  It actually works well in this image.  Good luck in the challenge!', '2019-09-03 04:11:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640261, 1240172, 6804, '<td valign="top">Great coloring and use of negative space here.  Excellent lead-lines to bring your eyes back to the boat.  Nice work.</td>', 'Great coloring and use of negative space here.  Excellent lead-lines to bring your eyes back to the boat.  Nice work.', '2019-09-03 04:13:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640263, 1240418, 6804, '<td valign="top">Nice coloring in this.  Soft sky and crisp detail in the water.  A great job of positioning the subjects as well.</td>', 'Nice coloring in this.  Soft sky and crisp detail in the water.  A great job of positioning the subjects as well.', '2019-09-03 04:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640264, 1240115, 6804, '<td valign="top">I love the image!  I''m not so hot on the title though.   "Backside" only tells me what side I''m looking at.  It doesn''t say anything at all about a "Boat".    I think if you had named it "Cargo" or something like "Headed to the Dock"  it might help the image associate better with a "Boat" in the eyes of a viewer.   It''s a great shot just the same!    Good Luck!</td>', 'I love the image!  I''m not so hot on the title though.   "Backside" only tells me what side I''m looking at.  It doesn''t say anything at all about a "Boat".    I think if you had named it "Cargo" or something like "Headed to the Dock"  it might help the image associate better with a "Boat" in the eyes of a viewer.   It''s a great shot just the same!    Good Luck!', '2019-09-03 04:31:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7640265, 1240421, 6804, '<td valign="top">I can see the "Boat"  i don''t think is a strong enough boat to boost you to the blue ribbon, however.  The image itself has a lot of style.  I hope the other voters hang out long enough to see the boat.... sadly i don''t think many of them will.... <br/>Good luck!   It''s certainly a bold image for a challenge shot.</td>', 'I can see the "Boat"  i don''t think is a strong enough boat to boost you to the blue ribbon, however.  The image itself has a lot of style.  I hope the other voters hang out long enough to see the boat.... sadly i don''t think many of them will.... Good luck!   It''s certainly a bold image for a challenge shot.', '2019-09-03 04:37:10.000000', NULL, 1),
